{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-114173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{t}{8}\\,\\text{d}t=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{t}{8}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{2}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}\\cdot {t}^{2}\\,{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(9-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114173" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114173" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{16}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  & =-3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0] \\\\  & =3(0-1) \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{5}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{arctan}\\,x\\,{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =5(\\text{arctan}(\\sqrt{3})-\\text{arctan}(1)) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =5(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339842" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-339842" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339842" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\pi}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}5{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}5{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot {e}^{x}\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =5({e}^{3}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =5({e}^{3}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-339791" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339791" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5e^3-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =3(arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339843" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-339843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339843" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(y-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{2}+\\frac{1}{y}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})+(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3)+(\\frac{1}{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}({e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,{|}_{1}^{e}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =({e}^{e}-{e}^{1})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =({e}^{e}-e)-(1-0) \\\\  & ={e}^{e}-e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339850" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-339850" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-339850" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^e-e-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}(2\\cdot {3}^{x}+x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the sum of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2\\cdot {3}^{x}+x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}({3}^{1}-{3}^{0})+\\frac{1}{2}({1}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(3-1)+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340324" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-340324" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340324" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{\\ln(3)}+\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-316004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-316004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}({x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|\\,{|}_{1}^{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(({e}^{2})^{3}-{1}^{3})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({e}^{6}-1)-(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}-1}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}-7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-316004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-316004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-316004" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{e^6}{3}-\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{7}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{7}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{7}(-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{7/2}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7/2}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{7}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{14}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-2}^{14}({x}^{2}-{e}^{x})\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-73343" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{7}{e}^{x}\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3z+2)\\,\\text{d}z.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(3z+2)\\,\\text{d}z & =3{\\int }_{-2}^{2}z\\,\\text{d}z+2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}{|}_{-2}^{2}+2z\\,{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2})+2(2-(-2)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-2008" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{3}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{3}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({3}^{4}-(-1)^{4})+2({3}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(81-1)+2(9-1) \\\\  & =20+16 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340354" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-340354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340354" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "36"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{8}-3)\\,\\text{d}t=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{8}-3)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{8}\\,\\text{d}t-3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{9}\\,{|}_{-1}^{1}-3t\\,{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}({1}^{9}-(-1)^{9})-3(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(1+1)-3(1+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}-6 \\\\  & =-\\frac{52}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{39}{16}"] ["math" "-\\frac{43}{18}"] ["math" "-\\frac{52}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{41}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{64}{27}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{52}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-2}^{1}(6{z}^{2}-5{z}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}(6{z}^{2}-5{z}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z & =6{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z-5{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{z}^{4}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1}-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}{z}^{5}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =2{z}^{3}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1}-{z}^{5}\\,{|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =2({1}^{3}-(-2)^{3})-({1}^{5}-(-2)^{5}) \\\\  & =2(1+8)-(1+32) \\\\  & =18-33 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-10"] ["math" "-15"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114190" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4{x}^{2}-6)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4{x}^{2}-6)\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-6{\\int }_{-1}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-6x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})-6(2-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(8-(-1))-6(3) \\\\  & =12-18 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-340395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}})\\text{d}y={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}(2-3{y}^{-2})\\text{d}y & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\text{d}y-3{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{y}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}-3(-{y}^{-1}){|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2y\\,{|}_{-2}^{-1}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{y}{|}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =2(-1-(-2))+3(\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{(-2)}) \\\\  & =2(-1+2)+3(-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2(1)+3(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-114202" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x){|}_{0}^{\\pi }+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =2[(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0)]+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =2(1-(-1))+(0-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340437" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-340437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340437" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}}+\\frac{x}{10})\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{{x}^{3}}}+\\frac{x}{10})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{16}(10{x}^{-3/4}+\\frac{1}{10}x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{16}(10{x}^{-3/4}+\\frac{1}{10}x)\\,\\text{d}x & =10{\\int }_{1}^{16}{x}^{-3/4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{10}{\\int }_{1}^{16}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4{x}^{1/4}\\,{|}_{1}^{16}+\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{16} \\\\  & =40{x}^{1/4}\\,{|}_{1}^{16}+\\frac{1}{20}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{16} \\\\  & =40({16}^{1/4}-{1}^{1/4})+\\frac{1}{20}({16}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =40(2-1)+\\frac{1}{20}(256-1) \\\\  & =40+\\frac{51}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{211}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{211}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{211}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{211}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{211}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{211}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29784" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{211}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{4}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{x}^{3/2}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of three integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(2{x}^{3/2}+3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{4}{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{x}^{5/2}{|}_{0}^{4}+3\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{4}+x\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}{x}^{5/2}{|}_{0}^{4}+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{4}+x\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}({4}^{5/2}-{0}^{5/2})+\\frac{3}{2}({4}^{2}-{0}^{2})+(4-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot 32+\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 16+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{128}{5}+28 \\\\  & =\\frac{268}{5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "28"] ["math" "54"] ["math" "\\frac{128}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{268}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{268}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-29780" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{268}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{x}}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{x}^{-1/2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{x}^{-1/2}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =6{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =6\\cdot 2{x}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =12{x}^{1/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =12({4}^{1/2}-{1}^{1/2})+\\frac{1}{3}({4}^{3}-{1}^{3}) \\\\  & =12(2-1)+\\frac{1}{3}(64-1) \\\\  & =12+21 \\\\  & =33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "df5804fa0cd2dbf5d2ed14816648487d535b3bab92912a14f3de3f5cbde52286"} {"question" "q-340422" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "q-340422" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "33"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/state.json" "file_sha256" "5642a27cc1464c23f68c52958dda89d3badefff031f72cb695fe650d857bebfe"} {"question" "e-413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-413.json" "file_sha256" "8f27df4572db30d50f56f1792fab15cdae8839f7a60f5903ef0ed6f1fa94075a"} {"question" "e-413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =3(8-(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-413.json" "file_sha256" "8f27df4572db30d50f56f1792fab15cdae8839f7a60f5903ef0ed6f1fa94075a"} {"question" "e-414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/4} (\\sec x \\tan x - \\cos x)\\, \\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-414.json" "file_sha256" "6bd51ea7ef3fe429d05ba3ff9633e107ac2982587176141bcf6fac15f3cf5ce6"} {"question" "e-414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sec}⁡0)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}-1)-(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-414.json" "file_sha256" "6bd51ea7ef3fe429d05ba3ff9633e107ac2982587176141bcf6fac15f3cf5ce6"} {"question" "e-415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^2(2x^3 - 5)\\, \\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-415.json" "file_sha256" "3de7cbb29e37ba5e411401fb62d5ce6d0141f6384630b09cb4fed6fe3e971626"} {"question" "e-415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(2{x}^{3}-5)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{-2}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-2}^{2}-5x\\,{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{4}-(-2)^{4})-5(2-(-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(16-16)-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-415.json" "file_sha256" "3de7cbb29e37ba5e411401fb62d5ce6d0141f6384630b09cb4fed6fe3e971626"} {"question" "e-416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm d x .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-416.json" "file_sha256" "6bd6f103540c1ea88f898dba142f231b9b362442d2793eea42247f574f35c7dc"} {"question" "e-416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_1^4 \\left( \\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_1^4 \\left( x^{1/2}-2x^{-2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx.\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+2{x}^{-1}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2})+2({4}^{-1}-{1}^{-1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1)+2(\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}+2\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004086/example-416.json" "file_sha256" "6bd6f103540c1ea88f898dba142f231b9b362442d2793eea42247f574f35c7dc"}] "usage" {"e-416" [] "e-413" [] "q-29784" [] "e-414" [] "e-415" []} "basis" 1092 "retractions" [[17592186115638 :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{16}(\\frac{10}{\\sqrt[4]{x^{3}}} + \\frac{x}{10})dx$?"] [17592186114946 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{2} 9 x^2 \\, \\textrm d x$."] [17592186114946 :question/worked-solution "Factoring the constant out of the integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-1}^{2}9x^{2}dx &= 9\\int_{-1}^{2}x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{3}}{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.3x^{3}\\right|_{-1}^{2} \\\\\n&= 3(2^{3} - (-1)^{3}) \\\\\n&= 3(8 - (-1)) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 9 \\\\\n&= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114953 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\pi/4} (\\sec x \\tan x - \\cos x)\\, \\textrm d x$."] [17592186114953 :question/worked-solution "Splitting up the integral into the difference of two integrals and evaluating each integral separately, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{π/4}(\\sec x\\tan x - \\cos x)dx &= \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\sec x\\tan xdx - \\int_{0}^{π/4}\\cos xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\sec x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} - \\left.\\sin x\\right|_{0}^{π/4} \\\\\n&= (\\sec \\frac{π}{4} - \\sec 0) - (\\sin \\frac{π}{4} - \\sin 0) \\\\\n&= (\\sqrt{2} - 1) - (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\sqrt{2} - \\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1 \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} - 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114958 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^2(2x^3 - 5)\\, \\textrm d x$."] [17592186114958 :question/worked-solution "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{-2}^{2}(2x^{3} - 5)dx &= 2\\int_{-2}^{2}x^{3}dx - 5\\int_{-2}^{2}1dx \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{1}{2}x^{4}\\right|_{-2}^{2} - \\left.5x\\right|_{-2}^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(2^{4} - (-2)^{4}) - 5(2 - (-2)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(16 - 16) - 5 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&=-20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114964 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{4} \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm d x$."] [17592186114964 :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int_1^4 \\left(\\sqrt x - \\dfrac 2 {x^2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx = \\int_1^4 \\left(x^{1/2}-2x^{-2} \\right) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\nThen, we split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{x} - \\frac{2}{x^{2}})dx &= \\int_{1}^{4}x^{1/2}dx - 2\\int_{1}^{4}x^{-2}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}\\right|_{1}^{4} + \\left.2x^{-1}\\right|_{1}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(4^{3/2} - 1^{3/2}) + 2(4^{-1} - 1^{-1}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{3}(8 - 1) + 2(\\frac{1}{4} - 1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} + 2 \\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{14}{3} - \\frac{3}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{19}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186113229 17592186113230 17592186113231 17592186113232 17592186113233] "immutable_fields" [[17592186113228 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113228 :answer-field/id] [17592186113228 :answer-field/key] [17592186113228 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
